    "walk": {
      "description": "carrying it into range. Six legs on an alternating tripod — front and back of one side swinging with the middle of the other, the two sets half a cycle apart — which is the gait the leg count implies and the one that reads as walking rather than as paddling. The prod breathes against its own tension over the top of it, because a loaded bow is never slack, and the barb rides a little of the draw down its groove: the pair is carried, not dragged. The two organs pulse out of phase with each other, because they are two animals.\n\nThis used to be a held pose on the theory that the pair does not walk. It does — the approach is most of the time it is alive, and it spent all of that standing still.",
