    "fuse": {
      "description": "landed, and filling. Four pumps across the half-second, each one leaving the sac bigger than the last let it settle back to — so the shape is a ratchet rather than a pulse, and what you read is pressure going in rather than a light blinking. It peaks on the final frame at three quarters again its own size, because the frame after this one is the blast. The core runs ahead of the sac the whole way, since the core is what is swelling and the sac is only what is failing to contain it, and it dims on each intake and comes back brighter — the one thing here that still reads at 1.35x on a crowded screen. The point is pushed out as the sac takes it, so it stays proud of the thing consuming it.\n\nThe sac is authored about its own middle, which is the only reason a scale on it is a swell rather than a stretch along the body. Its duration is the game's fuse; feelers stretches playback to `fuseTime`, so re-timing one re-times the other.\n\nOnly ever baked under `planted`. On the base body it would be a bow that never let go watching its own barb fill, which is not a state this creature has.",
