    "coil": {
      "description": "the windup, stretched to the game's telegraph. The barb hauls back down the groove while both limbs roll under the load and the core swells — the load is the only thing left saying a throw is coming, now that there is no string to draw. All six legs plant against it at the same time: feet dug in behind their joints and the stance opened wider than the one it walks on, because the throw goes forward and the recoil goes back, and a body that does not brace for that would simply be pushed off its own line. Wound rather than eased: a fast first draw, a slow creep against the load, a settle, a last snatch. Holds on the final frame, because the release is the throw.",
